    "classification": "third_country_to_eu_with_cplp_facilitation",
    "description": "Brazilian nationals are third-country nationals for Portuguese immigration. The CPLP (Comunidade dos Países de Língua Portuguesa) Mobility Agreement provides a distinctive facilitated pathway — a CPLP Residence Authorization — alongside the standard D2 (work/entrepreneur) and D7 (passive income / retirement) national visas. Since 2024 SEF was replaced by AIMA (Agência para a Integração, Migrações e Asilo)."
  },
  "fetched_at": "2026-06-04",
  "next_review_due": "2026-12-04",
  "regulatory_notes": [
    "SEF was dissolved in October 2023; AIMA is the successor authority (Decreto-Lei n.º 41/2023).",
    "Law 9/2025 of 13 February — CPLP Residence Authorization is now issued in the uniform EU residence-permit model.",
    "Article 77.º of Lei n.º 23/2007 — general residence-permit requirements."
  ],
